# Warehouse Management System

## 📌 Project Overview

The Warehouse Management System (WMS) is designed to modernize and optimize warehouse operations through automation, real-time inventory visibility, order processing, and data-driven management.

The system aims to reduce manual work, minimize inventory errors, improve warehouse productivity, and support efficient receiving, storage, picking, packing, shipping, and reporting.

## 🎯 Main Objectives

* Automate warehouse operations
* Maintain accurate inventory records
* Track stock in real time
* Improve warehouse space utilization
* Reduce order processing time
* Improve picking and shipping accuracy
* Support analytics and reporting
* Provide role-based system access

## 🚀 Main Features

### 1. Receiving Management

* Record received goods
* Barcode/RFID-based item scanning
* Quantity and batch verification
* Quality inspection
* Storage location assignment

### 2. Inventory Management

* Real-time stock tracking
* FIFO/LIFO support
* Batch and expiry management
* Stock adjustment
* Cycle counting

### 3. Storage & Location Management

* Warehouse location management
* Location mapping
* Storage assignment
* Capacity-based slotting

### 4. Order Management

* Create and modify orders
* Order prioritization
* Order status tracking
* Order processing

### 5. Picking

* Automatic pick-list generation
* Barcode confirmation
* Picking instructions
* Picking verification

### 6. Packing & Shipping

* Pick verification
* Packing confirmation
* Shipping label generation
* Shipment tracking

### 7. Returns Management

* Return receiving
* Return inspection
* Return reason recording
* Restocking/disposal processing

### 8. Analytics & Reporting

* Operational dashboard
* Daily/weekly/monthly reports
* KPI monitoring
* Inventory analytics

## 👥 User Roles

* Admin
* Warehouse Manager
* Inventory Officer
* Warehouse Staff
* Quality Control Officer
* Supply Chain Officer
* Picker
* Packing Staff
* Dispatch Officer

